# build-material-inline — notes arrive in the first message; Template A is skipped, Template C asks only open context rows
IFS= read -r -d '' PROMPT <<'PROMPT_EOF' || true
Use the interview-rehearsal skill. Here are my notes on my current project.

I joined Nissan in May 2024 as a senior Java developer, remote, contract. The system is a parts inventory platform: the system of record for how many of each part exist, at which facility, in which state, from suppliers to about 11 distribution centers to thousands of dealers. It's part of a broader monolith-to-microservices migration on AWS. Four adapter services take in feeds (3 streaming, 1 nightly batch), publish to Kafka, an Inventory Ledger service moves counts between states, replenishment Lambdas (MSK trigger) propose purchases to procurement, and a stock query service serves reads. Platform does 1-2 million events a day; low-stock events are hundreds a day. Team is 8: me, 4 other backend devs (2 senior, 2 junior), 1 QA, 1 PM, 1 team lead. PM and lead are internal, the rest are contract. I built the WMS adapter first, worked on the ledger, and own the replenishment Lambdas end to end. I recommended Lambda because the workload is sporadic, bursty and latency tolerant. I did not work on the stock query service.
PROMPT_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST <<'MUST_EOF' || true
Interviewers ask about context first
Why was this work happening
Who consumes what the system produces
"Don't know" is a fine answer
MUST_EOF
IFS= read -r -d '' MUST_NOT <<'MUST_NOT_EOF' || true
